1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,200
Welcome to the live demonstration of Sentinel AI for Gujarat Police.

2
00:00:04,200 --> 00:00:08,800
We begin on the main Surveillance command dashboard.

3
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:14,500
At the top, our KPI stats bar displays live operational counters:

4
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:20,200
Active city cameras, video streams, daily ANPR detections, and hotlist matches.

5
00:00:20,200 --> 00:00:26,000
On the left, live CCTV feeds; on the right, real-time incoming alert feeds.

6
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:31,800
Running 100% on-premises with zero external cloud API costs.

7
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:37,500
Here in the Live Camera Grid, we ingest multi-vendor RTSP streams

8
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:43,200
via our low-latency MediaMTX proxy: Hikvision, Dahua, CP Plus, and Axis.

9
00:00:43,200 --> 00:00:49,500
Operators can monitor multiple simultaneous junctions like SG Highway and Ashram Road.

10
00:00:49,500 --> 00:00:55,200
Our dual-head YOLOv8 and PaddleOCR pipeline runs continuously on-premises,

11
00:00:55,200 --> 00:01:00,500
detecting vehicles and enhancing plate crops with CLAHE contrast filtering,

12
00:01:00,500 --> 00:01:05,800
reading Indian license plates with over 97% recognition accuracy.

13
00:01:05,800 --> 00:01:11,000
Now, a red-flagged vehicle passes the SG Highway checkpoint.

14
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:17,200
In under 400ms, our in-memory Redis hotlist engine detects a critical match

15
00:01:17,200 --> 00:01:22,500
for FIR-2026-9081 — a reported stolen white SUV.

16
00:01:22,500 --> 00:01:28,000
The operator receives an instant audio-visual siren on the right sidebar,

17
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:33,500
displaying plate GJ 01 AB 1234, snapshot crops, and location details.

18
00:01:33,500 --> 00:01:38,500
The operator can click Acknowledge to confirm the incident

19
00:01:38,500 --> 00:01:41,100
and immediately alert field PCR patrol units.

20
00:01:41,100 --> 00:01:46,800
Next, clicking on Trajectory & GIS opens our spatial tracking module.

21
00:01:46,800 --> 00:01:52,500
We enter suspect license plate GJ 01 AB 1234 and click Search.

22
00:01:52,500 --> 00:01:58,500
The system queries PostGIS and reconstructs the vehicle's chronological journey.

23
00:01:58,500 --> 00:02:05,000
The map draws numbered breadcrumbs from stop 1 to stop 4,

24
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:12,300
showing directional headings, transit times, and average speeds.

25
00:02:12,300 --> 00:02:18,000
On the Suspect Hotlist tab, operators manage active FIR records

26
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:23,500
and perform bulk CSV uploads synchronized with CCTNS.

27
00:02:23,500 --> 00:02:30,000
The Cameras tab allows registering new RTSP camera endpoints with GPS coordinates.

28
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:37,000
Sentinel AI is 100% self-hosted, air-gapped compatible, with zero recurring fees.

29
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:42,600
Thank you for watching the Sentinel AI demonstration.

